==Portuguese==
{{wikipedia|lang=pt}}
[[file:Brazil State Alagoas.svg|thumb|Alagoas]]

===Etymology===
From {{m|pt|alagoas||lakes}}, variant form of {{m|pt|lagoa|t=lake}}.

The name appears as a competitor with the names of the lagoons of [[Manguaba]], {{m|pt||a lagoa do sul|t=the southern lagoon}}, and [[Mundaú]], {{m|pt||a lagoa do norte|t=the northern lagoon}}, already in the 16th century, when settlements were founded near the Alagoa do Norte and the Alagoa do Sul, the Alagoas, with the inclusion of the rest of the lagoons in the area.

